So after ascending a monk (no wielded weapons, vegetarian, armorless)
(8 classes down, 5 to go) I fired up a samurai.  She was level 5 with
50-some HP and a zero-ish AC by the time she found the mines, so she
drops down into the mines.  Wanders down a longish narrow corrider,
there's just a small room at the end, when suddently "a wave of psychic
energy washes over you!".  Crap.  Coming down the corrider is a master
mind flayer; having no means of digging or teleport, I wrote Elbereth
in the dust and fired arrows and my only wand (of sleep) feverishly.
Somehow the dust got disturbed, and a brief mind-suck later I was dead.

Master mind flayer on DL5?  Yikes.  I'm not sure how I could avert
that, though; I was trying to watch the Elbereth on the floor and keep
it at bay for arrows, but apparently I can't control the dust well
enough to make that a workable strategy.  Also had 2 unID'd potions,
some boots that weren't ID'd but I was pretty sure were water-walking
(right price, not speed, couldn't jump)

My very next character dropped into the mines and recognized a familiar
looking bones level with psychic energy scanning the level.  Haha.  I
have the advantage this time: I can come down the corrider with _you_
trapped, easy running distance to the stairs, and I'm carrying
/Lightning and /Fire.  One barbecued MMF later, I'm holding a
/polymorph (explaining the out-of-depth monster) and a bunch of stuff
from the previous samurai (including water walking boots).  Minetown is
just 3 levels deep, and both of the levels above it are lit.

So I pop into the general store and find a 750-Zorkmid wand (Cha 7 is a
bad thing).  Lining up the shopkeeper, I zap the wand and "You may wish
for an object".  Let's see, 2 blessed ?Charging to start.  I could
rustle up a /Death to deal with the keeper, but I decide that a charge
from the /Poly is a better use.  After killing the resultant long worm
and taking its wands/potions/key, I go back to wishing--no charges
left, so I recharge it and get:

Blessed greased +0 SDSM
Blessed Magic Mirror of Merlin
Blessed +3 Grayswandir
Blessed fireproof +3 speed boots.

Until the monk I'd avoided wishing for artifacts, but this role seems a
little boring and so I figured I'd try to munchkin her out as much as
possible.

I'm not sure that was the optimal usage, but I decided that I should go
for reflection and MR _now_ to maximize survivability, and I've never
had Grayswandir so I wanted to give it a try (and wanted to wish for it
before more artifacts were created).

I'd already found a bag of holding, and have since found a huge scroll
shop netting 9 identify, 5 enchant armor, and 3 enchant weapon scrolls,
an armor shop with leather gloves and cloak of displacement, and some
misc. niceties (poison/fire/cold resistance, unihorn, =conflict, lizard
corpse, etc).  I could use some /teleport or other emergency supplies.
Could also use an altar to get holy water for the scrolls (Minetown is
cross-aligned).  #twoweaponing Grayswandir and a katana is nice.

I guess most YAAD are off the table now, so this one'll probably be a
YASD.

After my last few roles (rogue, monk, ranger), samurai sure seem easy
(at least in the early game).  I also have healer, priest, knight, and
barbarian remaining.



